## Enrollment
Junction between Student and Section. Grade is nullable — assigned after course completion.
FK chain depth: Department → Course → Section → Enrollment (3 hops from root).
A student can enroll in a section only once (unique constraint).

## Prerequisite
Self-referencing junction on Course: both course_id and prereq_id point to Course.
Forms a DAG — cycles would mean a course requires itself (enforced by application).
Used to validate enrollment eligibility before admitting students to sections.

## Student
advisor_id is nullable — not all students have an assigned advisor (e.g., freshmen).
total_credits is a denormalized count, updated as enrollments with passing grades are recorded.

## Section
Semester+year composite index for term-based queries. Building/room/time_slot nullable for TBD scheduling.
